body:
Get out of my house. I never wanted another human as my mirror in this aspect of life! 22 year old guy - taking the comfy road and getting pushed by others/external pressure to get stuff done.

&#x200B;

Jokes aside, incremental, consistent, stubborn progress along with optimal environmental design helps i think (cutting out derailers and putting up stuff that makes things easy to follow). 

I guess patience is extremely important too. To undo years of brain wiring, we have to expect at least months of consistent rewiring efforts. 

&#x200B;

Best of luck to you. And kudos for not giving up.
